# NEN 2660-2 relation profile — the characteristics NEN 2660-2's RDFS does not
# declare, chosen per Keet et al. (OntoPartS): choosing the wrong part-whole
# relation, or making the wrong one transitive, yields wrong inferences (a pump
# *contained in* a service building is not *part of* the building; a pump's
# housing *is* part of the pump, and so of the pumping station).
#
# Only proper parthood (hasPart and its functional/technical sub-relations,
# which inherit transitivity through rdfs:subPropertyOf) is transitive.
# Irreflexivity and acyclicity are NOT declared here: OWL 2 DL forbids
# irreflexive/asymmetric on a transitive property, so they are SHACL shapes
# (shapes.ttl). Containment, constitution and connection are not transitive.
#
# The relation IRIs and their English labels are NEN 2660-2:2022's (© NEN,
# which grants no licence; its files are fetched, never vendored — see
# manifest.toml). The characteristics and the scope notes are this project's
# own words, not NEN's definitions, and NEN has not published or endorsed
# this profile.
@prefix nen2660: <https://w3id.org/nen2660/def#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix prof:    <https://example.org/nen2660-relations/profile#> .

prof: a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "NEN 2660-2 relation profile"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "OWL characteristics for the NEN 2660-2 part-whole, containment, constitution and connection relations. Transitivity only on proper parthood; irreflexivity, acyclicity and spatial consistency are shapes."@en .

# ── Decomposition (parthood) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

nen2660:hasPart a owl:ObjectProperty , owl:TransitiveProperty ;
    rdfs:label "has part"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Proper parthood: the deck is part of the bridge, the bearing part of the deck, so — transitively — the bearing is part of the bridge. Never reflexive, never cyclic (shapes)."@en .

nen2660:hasFunctionalPart a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf nen2660:hasPart ;
    rdfs:label "has functional part"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "The functional decomposition: a pumping station's function has the pumping function as part. Transitive through hasPart, not on its own."@en .

nen2660:hasTechnicalPart a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:subPropertyOf nen2660:hasPart ;
    rdfs:label "has technical part"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "The technical (physical) decomposition: the housing is a technical part of the pump. Transitive through hasPart, not on its own."@en .

# ── Containment (location, not parthood) ────────────────────────────────────

nen2660:contains a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "contains"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Location: a spatial region (a room, a service area) holds whatever sits inside it. Location is not parthood: the pump in the service building is contained in it, not part of it, and containment does not chain through parts. Not transitive; irreflexive by shape; a contained object lies within the region's geometry (shape)."@en .

# ── Constitution ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

nen2660:consistsOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "consists of"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Constitution: what something is made of — a beam of steel, a deck of concrete. Constitution is not parthood: the steel is not a part of the beam. Not transitive."@en .

# ── Connection ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

nen2660:connectsObject a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "connects object"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Joining: a coupling, weld or other interface ties two objects together — a pipe to a pump, a girder to a bearing. No hierarchy, no transitivity; a connection never connects an object to itself (shape)."@en .

nen2660:connectsPort a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "connects port"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Joining at a port: the interface ties specific ports together (a pump's outlet to a pipe's inlet) rather than whole objects. No hierarchy, no transitivity."@en .
